WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.160
Hi, my name is Neerja Aggarwal.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.740
I'm a graduate student here
at MIT in the physical optics

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:06.090
and electronics lab.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:08.790
Our lab is trying to do
noninvasive diagnostics using

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.050
spectroscopy.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:11.550
Raman spectroscopy
is a technique

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:13.980
in which you shine
laser light at a sample

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.790
and measure the
scattered photons.

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:18.264
Now, this gives you a spectral
fingerprint of the molecule.

00:00:18.264 --> 00:00:19.680
Clinical trials
have already shown

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.630
this to be an effective
technique for cancer

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:25.230
diagnostics, but we need
a way to develop and test

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.150
new instruments in
the laboratory setting

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.970
before jumping to
expensive clinical trials.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.560
During my master's
research, I showed

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.630
that you can use an
in vitro skin tissue

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.780
culture as an optical
substitute for human skin

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.659
instead of jumping
to clinical trials.

00:00:38.659 --> 00:00:40.200
I showed that the
skin tissue culture

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.480
has similar Raman,
autofluorescence,

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.910
and optical properties
as human skin

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.700
with more than 25
volunteers as comparison,

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.090
making it an
invaluable R&amp;D tool.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:51.840
Now, another challenge
with this technique

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.870
is that you're measuring
a really small Raman

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:57.120
signal on top of a large
autofluorescence background.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.850
I looked at ways to separate
these two signals in time

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:02.340
using time-correlated
single photon counting,

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.129
thereby improving the
signal to noise ratio.

00:01:05.129 --> 00:01:06.720
Now, Raman
spectroscopy is already

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.570
undergoing commercialization,
and these two results

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:11.950
will accelerate the product
development process,

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:14.316
bringing it closer to patients.

